{"type":"tool_execution_update","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01ARJ7vt2huHM1uvYCe4Fhhn","toolName":"subagent","args":{"agent":"refactor","agentScope":"both","task":"Test file: src/game-of-life.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/game-of-life.ts\nPassing tests: 9 (all tests complete)\nRecent changes: Added blinker oscillator tests, block still life, and survival tests -- all passing with existing neighbor-counting implementation.\n\nRefactor the complete implementation while keeping all 9 tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."},"partialResult":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Step 5: New APP Mass\n\n**Extracted `parseCellKey` function:**\n```ts\nconst parseCellKey = (key: string): Cell => key.split(\",\").map(Number) as Cell;\n```\n- Bindings: `key`, `Number` = 2\n- Invocations: `split(...)`, `map(...)` = 2 → mass 4\n- Constants: `\",\"` = 1\n- Total: **7**\n\n**Call site now:**\n```ts\nnextCells.push(parseCellKey(k));\n```\n- Bindings: `k` = 1\n- Invocations: `push(...)`, `parseCellKey(...)` = 2 → mass 4\n- Total: **5**\n\nCombined new mass ≈ 7 + 5 = **12** vs. old localized **9** for the inline parse plus the `push` invocation (2) = 11.\n\n**Mass Change:** ~11 → ~12 (delta +1). Mass rose marginally due to the extra invocation of the named function.\n\n## Step 6: Decision\n\n**Refactoring Applied — Extract `parseCellKey` helper**\n\n- **Naming:** All existing names already revealed intent and were kept. The one gap was the missing inverse of `cellKey`; introduced `parseCellKey` to complete the symmetric serialize/deserialize pair.\n- **Rule 2 (Reveals intent) — primary win:** The final loop now reads `nextCells.push(parseCellKey(k))` instead of an inline `k.split(\",\").map(Number)`, making the round-trip relationship with `cellKey` explicit and self-documenting.\n- **Rule 3 (No duplication):** The `\",\"` key-format literal was conceptually duplicated (once in `cellKey`, once inline). Knowledge of the key format now lives next to its counterpart, establishing single representation of the concept.\n- **APP note:** Mass increased by ~1 due to the added function invocation. Per the guideline **Rule 2 trumps APP**, the clarity and DRY gains justify the negligible mass cost.\n\n## Step 7: Report\n\n**Refactoring Complete**\n- **Refactoring:** Extracted `parseCellKey` as the named inverse of `cellKey`, replacing an inline `split`/`map`. Improves Rule 2 (intent) and Rule 3 (single representation of key format).\n- **Mass Change:** ~11 → ~12 (+1) — accepted; clarity trumps APP.\n- **Tests:** All 9 passing. ✅"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_05-52-18_game-of-life-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_opus-4-8-2/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/game-of-life.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/game-of-life.ts\nPassing tests: 9 (all tests complete)\nRecent changes: Added blinker oscillator tests, block still life, and survival tests -- all passing with existing neighbor-counting implementation.\n\nRefactor the complete implementation while keeping all 9 tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/game-of-life.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/game-of-life.ts\nPassing tests: 9 (all tests complete)\nRecent changes: Added blinker oscillator tests, block still life, and survival tests -- all passing with existing neighbor-counting implementation.\n\nRefactor the complete implementation while keeping all 9 tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784959098701},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Looking at the implementation and test files to understand how everything works together.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01PaMjtZJjUYo9JR1cATnvJ1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_05-52-18_game-of-life-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_opus-4-8-2/src/game-of-life.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01YFqWXg1VQYTxY1mm6SYPMV","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_05-52-18_game-of-life-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_opus-4-8-2/src/game-of-life.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":210,"output":255,"cacheRead":10360,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10825,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784959098721,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-cd780656-8aad-48fd-b69a-d6bb6ef95227","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01PaMjtZJjUYo9JR1cATnvJ1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"type Cell = [number, number]; // [x, y]\n\nconst cellKey = (x: number, y: number) => `${x},${y}`;\n\nfunction survivesToNextGeneration(isAlive: boolean, neighborCount: number): boolean {\n  return isAlive ? neighborCount === 2 || neighborCount === 3 : neighborCount === 3;\n}\n\nexport function nextGeneration(cells: Cell[]): Cell[] {\n  const alive = new Set(cells.map(([x, y]) => cellKey(x, y)));\n  const neighborCounts = new Map<string, number>();\n\n  for (const [x, y] of cells) {\n    for (let dx = -1; dx <= 1; dx++) {\n      for (let dy = -1; dy <= 1; dy++) {\n        if (dx === 0 && dy === 0) continue;\n        const k = cellKey(x + dx, y + dy);\n        neighborCounts.set(k, (neighborCounts.get(k) ?? 0) + 1);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  const nextCells: Cell[] = [];\n  for (const [k, neighborCount] of neighborCounts) {\n    if (survivesToNextGeneration(alive.has(k), neighborCount)) {\n      const [x, y] = k.split(\",\").map(Number);\n      nextCells.push([x, y]);\n    }\n  }\n  return nextCells;\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784959101403},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01YFqWXg1VQYTxY1mm6SYPMV","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { nextGeneration } from \"./game-of-life.js\";\n\nconst norm = (cells: [number, number][]) =>\n  [...cells].sort((a, b) => a[0] - b[0] || a[1] - b[1]);\n\ndescribe(\"Game of Life - Next Generation\", () => {\n  it(\"should return empty array for empty input\", () => {\n    expect(nextGeneration([])).toEqual([]);\n  });\n  it(\"should kill a single live cell -- [(0,0)] -> []\", () => {\n    expect(nextGeneration([[0, 0]])).toEqual([]);\n  });\n  it(\"Rule 1 Underpopulation: live cells with < 2 neighbors die -- [(0,1),(1,1)] -> []\", () => {\n    expect(nextGeneration([[0, 1], [1, 1]])).toEqual([]);\n  });\n  it(\"Rule 3 Overpopulation: live cell with > 3 neighbors dies -- center of full ring dies\", () => {\n    const gen0: [number, number][] = [[0, 0], [1, 0], [2, 0], [1, 1], [0, 2], [1, 2], [2, 2]];\n    const gen1: [number, number][] = [[0, 0], [0, 2], [1, -1], [1, 0], [1, 2], [1, 3], [2, 0], [2, 2]];\n    expect(norm(nextGeneration(gen0))).toEqual(norm(gen1));\n  });\n  it(\"Rule 4 Reproduction: dead cell with exactly 3 neighbors becomes alive\", () => {\n    const gen0: [number, number][] = [[0, 0], [1, 0], [0, 1]];\n    const gen1: [number, number][] = [[0, 0], [0, 1], [1, 0], [1, 1]];\n    expect(norm(nextGeneration(gen0))).toEqual(norm(gen1));\n  });\n  it(\"Block still life: [(0,0),(1,0),(0,1),(1,1)] stays unchanged\", () => {\n    const block: [number, number][] = [[0, 0], [1, 0], [0, 1], [1, 1]];\n    expect(norm(nextGeneration(block))).toEqual(norm(block));\n  });\n  it(\"Rule 2 Survival: center cell with 2 or 3 neighbors lives on\", () => {\n    // middle cell (1,0) has exactly 2 live neighbors -> survives\n    const gen0: [number, number][] = [[0, 0], [1, 0], [2, 0]];\n    const gen1: [number, number][] = [[1, -1], [1, 0], [1, 1]];\n    expect(norm(nextGeneration(gen0))).toEqual(norm(gen1));\n  });\n  it(\"Blinker oscillator gen0 -> gen1: [(0,0),(0,1),(0,2)] -> [(-1,1),(0,1),(1,1)]\", () => {\n    const gen0: [number, number][] = [[0, 0], [0, 1], [0, 2]];\n    const gen1: [number, number][] = [[-1, 1], [0, 1], [1, 1]];\n    expect(norm(nextGeneration(gen0))).toEqual(norm(gen1));\n  });\n  it(\"Blinker oscillator gen1 -> gen2 returns to vertical\", () => {\n    const gen1: [number, number][] = [[-1, 1], [0, 1], [1, 1]];\n    const gen2: [number, number][] = [[0, 0], [0, 1], [0, 2]];\n    expect(norm(nextGeneration(gen1))).toEqual(norm(gen2));\n  });\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784959101403},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me run the tests to make sure everything's passing.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_014ptoPqHkmoWQmvkAPFC4fm","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_05-52-18_game-of-life-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_opus-4-8-2 && pnpm test 2>&1 | tail -20"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":2188,"output":147,"cacheRead":10360,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":12695,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784959101403,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-817e12ec-a50e-40bc-bbd2-7537eed6cd31","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_014ptoPqHkmoWQmvkAPFC4fm","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_05-52-18_game-of-life-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_opus-4-8-2\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-25_05-52-18_game-of-life-example-mapping_v6.2.1-phase-continuation-pi_opus-4-8-2\n\n ✓ src/game-of-life.spec.ts  (9 tests) 4ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  9 passed (9)\n   Start at  05:58:24