arse representation, handles negative coordinates, and works on an infinite grid. `experiment-done.txt` written with `DONE`."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":1486,"output":378,"cacheRead":35185,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":37049,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784959145163,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-519b9f83-7df4-4e1d-bbe3-727c6fab0a32","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"}},"message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The TDD workflow is complete. Summary of the full autonomous run:\n\n**Test List** — 9 tests covering all 4 rules and every spec example (empty input, single cell, underpopulation, overpopulation, reproduction, block still life, survival, blinker gen0→1 and gen1→2).\n\n**Red/Green/Refactor cycles:**\n- Test 1 (empty → []): Red (compile+runtime failure predicted correctly) → Green (`return []`) → Refactor\n- Tests 2, 3: already passed with the trivial impl (skipped green/refactor)\n- Test 4 (overpopulation): Red (failure predicted) → Green (full neighbor-counting rules with Set + Map) → Refactor (extracted `survivesToNextGeneration`)\n- Tests 5–9: all passed with the complete rule implementation (skipped green/refactor)\n- Final refactor pass on the complete implementation (extracted `parseCellKey`)\n\nAll 9 tests pass. The implementation uses sparse representation, handles negative coordinates, and works on an infinite grid. `experiment-done.txt` written with `DONE`."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-opus-4-8@eu","usage":{"input":1486,"output":378,"cacheRead":35185,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":37049,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784959145163,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-519b9f83-7df4-4e1d-bbe3-727c6fab0a32","responseModel":"claude-opus-4-8"}}
